text.section:
Except as otherwise provided in this section, any reports, information, or records received or maintained by the Board regarding active investigations or disciplinary proceedings for violations of this chapter shall be strictly confidential. The Board may only disclose such confidential information:

In a disciplinary proceeding before a health regulatory board or in any subsequent trial or appeal of an action or order;


To the permittee when entering into a confidential consent agreement;


To regulatory authorities tasked with granting, limiting, or denying licenses, certificates, or registrations to practice a health profession;


Pursuant to a court order for good cause arising from extraordinary circumstances;


To qualified personnel for bona fide research or educational purposes, provided that identifying information is redacted and the information is released pursuant to a written agreement that ensures compliance with this section;


To the Health Practitioners' Monitoring Program within the Department of Health Professions for the purpose of evaluating health practitioners who have applied to or participate in the Program; or


To the Joint Legislative Audit and Review Commission pursuant to § 30-59.
